Subject: [PATCH] fix(lora): apply `|high_noise|` LoRAs when applied at runtime

A LoRA loaded for the high noise expert (`<lora:|high_noise|NAME:W>`) has its
tensors renamed to `lora.model.high_noise_diffusion_model.*`. When the weights
are quantized (GGUF Q4/Q5/Q8...) LoRAs are applied at runtime, and
apply_loras_at_runtime() only kept tensors named `model.diffusion_model.*`, so
the high noise LoRA was left empty and silently dropped: the video was
bit-identical with and without it.

Keep the high noise tensors too. The adapter is shared by both experts, which
is safe because every runner looks its weights up by its own prefix.

diff --git a/src/name_conversion.cpp b/src/name_conversion.cpp
index bd23231..9fa6cd6 100644
--- a/src/name_conversion.cpp
+++ b/src/name_conversion.cpp
@@ -1544,6 +1544,13 @@ bool is_diffusion_model_name(const std::string& name) {
     return false;
 }
 
+// Tensors of a LoRA loaded with the `|high_noise|` prefix are named
+// `lora.model.high_noise_diffusion_model.*` (see ModelManager::prepare_lora_sources).
+bool is_high_noise_diffusion_model_name(const std::string& name) {
+    static const std::string prefix = "model.high_noise_diffusion_model.";
+    return starts_with(name, prefix) || starts_with(name, "lora." + prefix);
+}
+
